{
  "id": "pipeline-feedback",
  "title": "A float history pipeline adds 1/16 per submission, and pause, step, capture, and reset act on submissions exactly",
  "binding": "The positive leg boots an offscreen world whose one pipeline accumulates previous.r + 1/16 into a zero-initialized 32x32 half-float history, converts it to opaque grayscale RGBA8, and copies it through a fullscreen pass. It waits for compilation and installation, pauses, resets, and captures the one initialization frame twice, steps once, steps fifteen more times, and resets again. Every interior pixel of each capture must sit within one code of 255 * min(n/16, 1) at submission n, computed from the arithmetic rather than recorded. The discriminating leg binds the accumulator's previous-frame input to a zero history nothing writes, so submissions 2 and 17 stay at 1/16 and the positive oracles turn red.",
